  "notes": "The bird logo is drawn as fin areas (its feathers) plus a logo entry, so a renderer can use either. When the scheme was introduced isn't dated here; it came with the A320neo family deliveries. The earlier scheme (white with a navy-and-blue fin) remains on A320ceo-family aircraft; not drawn. Belly under the forward fuselage white; aft navy. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on SX-NEB (A320neo, fitted to the A320 shape): 'AEGEAN' sits right on the window tops (y 0.28, it had floated higher), x 0.164-0.37; 'aegeanair.com' x 0.673-0.757; the diagonal agrees (reduced to its ends); the feathers drawn as curves.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation (blue belly, navy bands)."
